  "result": {
    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Indicators\"\ndescription: \"The 34 municipal indicators of the RESA-MT Observatory, grouped into six themes, with a map of the 141 municipalities of Mato Grosso, rankings within each biome and across the state, and a table showing the IBGE symbols\"\ntoc: false\npage-layout: full\n---\n\n\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"faixa-versao\">\nPreliminary version for the project team. Results may change as the study progresses.\n English translation under review. If the two versions differ, the Portuguese text prevails.\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe observatory covers 34 indicators, grouped into six themes, for the 141 municipalities of Mato Grosso (MT). Each indicator page has:\n\n- a **choropleth map** of the 141 municipalities, with classes based on quintiles and X shown in grey;\n- a **ranking** within each biome and across Mato Grosso, highlighting the three pilot-area host municipalities;\n- a **time series**, where available, for indicators from the Greenhouse Gas Emissions and Removals Estimation System (SEEG);\n- aggregates by biome and by Manuscript 1 (M1) type;\n- the **full table**, with a column for the symbols used by the Brazilian Institute of Geography and Statistics (IBGE) and an option to download the filtered rows.\n\nEach card shows the value for Mato Grosso: the municipal sum for totals, the ratio of sums for proportions and means, and the change in sums for dynamics indicators. Key indicators carry the [key]{.selo} badge.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"legenda-sinais\">\nIBGE standard symbols: \n<b>X</b>\n suppressed (value withheld to avoid identifying the respondent) · \n<b>–</b>\n true zero · \n<b>...</b>\n not available. None of these symbols is shown as zero.\n</div>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Structure of family farming {#estrutura}\n\nThese indicators use the number of establishments, area, persons employed and value of production to measure the size and relative importance of family farming in each municipality (IBGE, 2017 Agricultural Census). Indicators in this theme: 9.\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"lista-ind\">\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"estab_af.html\">\n    <h4>\n      Family farms\n      <span class=\"selo\">key</span>\n    </h4>\n    <p>establishments · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>81,635</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_estab_af.html\">\n    <h4>\n      Family-farm share of establishments\n      <span class=\"selo\">key</span>\n    </h4>\n    <p>% of agricultural establishments · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>68.8%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"area_af.html\">\n    <h4>Family-farm area</h4>\n    <p>hectares · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>5,131,101</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_area_af.html\">\n    <h4>Family-farm share of area</h4>\n    <p>% of the area of agricultural establishments · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>9.3%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"area_media_af.html\">\n    <h4>\n      Mean family-farm area\n      <span class=\"selo\">key</span>\n    </h4>\n    <p>hectares per establishment · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>62.9</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pessoal_af.html\">\n    <h4>Persons employed on family farms</h4>\n    <p>persons · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>215,693</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"valor_prod_af.html\">\n    <h4>\n      Value of family-farm production\n      <span class=\"selo\">key</span>\n    </h4>\n    <p>R$ (2017 values) · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>R$3.8 billion</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"sub\">1 municipality with X (suppressed)</p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"valor_prod_estab_af.html\">\n    <h4>Value of production per family farm</h4>\n    <p>R$ per establishment (2017 values) · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>R$46.4 thousand</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"sub\">1 municipality with X (suppressed)</p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_valor_animal_af.html\">\n    <h4>% of value from animal production</h4>\n    <p>% of the value of family-farm production · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>67.8%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"sub\">3 municipalities with X (suppressed)</p>\n  </a>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Technology, technical assistance and credit {#tecnologia}\n\nThis theme shows how widespread machinery, farming practices, electricity, technical guidance, financing and the PRONAF Eligibility Declaration (DAP) are among family farms (IBGE, 2017 Agricultural Census). Indicators in this theme: 8.\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"lista-ind\">\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_trator_af.html\">\n    <h4>% with tractor</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>15.4%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_plantio_direto_af.html\">\n    <h4>% using no-till</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>5.2%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_irrigacao_af.html\">\n    <h4>% with irrigation</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>4.2%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_energia_af.html\">\n    <h4>% with electricity</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>89.5%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_orientacao_af.html\">\n    <h4>% with technical guidance</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>12.5%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_financiamento_af.html\">\n    <h4>% with financing</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>15.9%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_pronaf_af.html\">\n    <h4>% with PRONAF</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>5.7%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_dap_af.html\">\n    <h4>% with DAP</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>25.2%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Production and food {#alimentos}\n\nThis theme describes the purpose and composition of family-farm production: own consumption, cow’s milk, cassava and horticulture (IBGE, 2017 Agricultural Census). Indicators in this theme: 4.\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"lista-ind\">\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_consumo_proprio_af.html\">\n    <h4>% producing for own consumption</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>28.2%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_leite_af.html\">\n    <h4>% producing milk</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>34.3%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_mandioca_af.html\">\n    <h4>% producing cassava</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>14.7%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_horticultura_af.html\">\n    <h4>% in horticulture and floriculture</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>2.0%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Tenure and agrarian reform {#posse}\n\nThis theme covers the producer’s land tenure status (IBGE, 2017 Agricultural Census) and the settlement projects of the National Institute for Colonisation and Agrarian Reform (INCRA). The projects are recorded in the Agrarian Reform Projects Information System (SIPRA, Report 0227, as at 3 June 2025). Category 46504 understates the extent of agrarian reform, and SIPRA counts each project only in its host municipality. Indicators in this theme: 7.\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"lista-ind\">\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"estab_af_46504.html\">\n    <h4>Family farms in 46504</h4>\n    <p>establishments · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>8,834</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_estab_46504.html\">\n    <h4>\n      % of family farms in 46504\n      <span class=\"selo\">key</span>\n    </h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>10.8%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_area_46504.html\">\n    <h4>% of family-farm area in 46504</h4>\n    <p>% of family-farm area · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>11.3%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n    <p class=\"sub\">52 municipalities with X (suppressed)</p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"pct_estab_prop_af.html\">\n    <h4>% run by owners</h4>\n    <p>% of family farms · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>84.8%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, ratio of municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"n_pa.html\">\n    <h4>Settlement projects</h4>\n    <p>projects · 2025</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>575</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"fam_pa.html\">\n    <h4>\n      Settled families\n      <span class=\"selo\">key</span>\n    </h4>\n    <p>families · 2025</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>85,653</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"area_pa.html\">\n    <h4>Project area</h4>\n    <p>hectares · 2025</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>6,539,004</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Climate (SEEG 13) {#clima}\n\nThis theme covers greenhouse gas emissions and removals estimated by SEEG 13 (GWP-AR5) for the whole municipality, not only for family farming. The series run from 1970 to 2024 for gross emissions and for agriculture and livestock emissions, and from 1990 to 2024 for land-use change and removals. Indicators in this theme: 4.\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"lista-ind\">\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"seeg_emissao_bruta.html\">\n    <h4>\n      Gross emissions\n      <span class=\"selo\">key</span>\n    </h4>\n    <p>thousand tCO2e (GWP-AR5) · 1970–2024</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>230,981.8</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"seeg_agropecuaria.html\">\n    <h4>Agriculture and livestock emissions</h4>\n    <p>thousand tCO2e (GWP-AR5) · 1970–2024</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>88,866.4</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"seeg_mut.html\">\n    <h4>Land-use change emissions</h4>\n    <p>thousand tCO2e (GWP-AR5) · 1990–2024</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>125,813.4</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"seeg_remocoes.html\">\n    <h4>Removals</h4>\n    <p>thousand tCO2e (GWP-AR5) · 1990–2024</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>59,261.5</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, municipal sum</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n</div>\n```\n\n## 2006–2017 dynamics {#dinamica}\n\nThese indicators measure the change in the number and area of all agricultural establishments (family and non-family farms) between the 2006 and 2017 Censuses. The 2006 municipal sum does not, however, match the state table. Indicators in this theme: 2.\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"lista-ind\">\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"var_estab_0617.html\">\n    <h4>\n      Change in establishments, 2006–2017\n      <span class=\"selo\">key</span>\n    </h4>\n    <p>% (2017 relative to 2006) · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>5.0%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, change in municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n  <a class=\"cartao cartao-ind\" href=\"var_area_0617.html\">\n    <h4>Change in area, 2006–2017</h4>\n    <p>% (2017 relative to 2006) · 2017</p>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.25rem\">\n      <b>12.8%</b>\n      <span class=\"sub\"> MT, change in municipal sums</span>\n    </p>\n  </a>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Comparison by biome and by M1 type\n\nThe tables below give the aggregates for each indicator in its reference year. Biomes follow the IBGE 1:250,000 map (2019) and types follow the Manuscript 1 typology (k = 5), whose labels are provisional. In groups with X, the aggregate covers only municipalities with a published value.\n\n::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n### Structure\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"reactable html-widget html-fill-item\" id=\"htmlwidget-9296e7759c514c125721\" style=\"width:auto;height:auto;\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-9296e7759c514c125721\">{\"x\":{\"tag\":{\"name\":\"Reactable\",\"attribs\":{\"data\":{\"Indicador\":[\"<a href=\\\"estab_af.html\\\">Family farms<\\/a><div class=\\\"sub\\\">establishments<\\/div>\",\"<a href=\\\"pct_estab_af.html\\\">Family-farm share of agricultural establishments<\\/a><div class=\\\"sub\\\">% of agricultural establishments<\\/div>\",\"<a href=\\\"area_af.html\\\">Family-farm area<\\/a><div class=\\\"sub\\\">hectares<\\/div>\",\"<a href=\\\"pct_area_af.html\\\">Family-farm share of the area of agricultural establishments<\\/a><div class=\\\"sub\\\">% of the area of agricultural establishments<\\/div>\",\"<a href=\\\"area_media_af.html\\\">Mean area of family farms<\\/a><div class=\\\"sub\\\">hectares per establishment<\\/div>\",\"<a href=\\\"pessoal_af.html\\\">Persons employed on family farms<\\/a><div class=\\\"sub\\\">persons<\\/div>\",\"<a href=\\\"valor_prod_af.html\\\">Value of family-farm production<\\/a><div class=\\\"sub\\\">R$ (2017 values)<\\/div>\",\"<a href=\\\"valor_prod_estab_af.html\\\">Value of production per family farm<\\/a><div class=\\\"sub\\\">R$ per establishment (2017 values)<\\/div>\",